  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th and Sarah Tan leading the project. The executive board has approved a total budget of $2M, which covers research, development, and marketing. Specific budget allocations include $500,000 for phase one, $55,000 for the compliance plan (including training and audits), and $15,000 for specialized training programs for the coding team and project managers. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Key developments include a breakthrough in predictive analytics in phase two, a call for AI-driven data visualization ideas by July 20th, and exploratory partnership discussions with TechInnovate. A detailed progress report will be shared on November 20th, and feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November."
